{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"OUDSTextInput","modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"platforms":[{"introducedAt":"15.0","name":"iOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"15.0","name":"macOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"1.0","name":"visionOS","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSTextInput"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSTextInput"}],"externalID":"s:14OUDSComponents13OUDSTextInputV","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/7SwiftUI4ViewP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Text input is a UI element that allows to enter, edit, or select single-line textual data."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Text input is one of the most fundamental form elements used to capture user input such as names, emails, passwords, or search queries."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It provides a visual and interactive affordance for text entry while supporting labels, placeholders, icons, descriptions, and validation feedback."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/Helperlink","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/TrailingAction"],"generated":true},{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/init(label:text:placeholder:prefix:suffix:leadingIcon:flipLeadingIcon:trailingAction:helperText:helperLink:isOutlined:constrainedMaxWidth:status:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/body"],"generated":true},{"title":"Enumerations","anchor":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/Status","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/Style"],"generated":true},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/View-Implementations","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTextInput\/View-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSTextInput"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/Controls"],"kind":"mentions"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Layout","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Layout"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Text input is based on several configurable UI elements:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"label"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": It is used to describe the purpose of the input.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In some UI contexts, especially when space is limited or when the input is part of a compact layout (search bars, filters, inline forms), the label can be hidden.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However, hiding the label should only be done if the purpose of the input remains clear thanks to a placeholder or contextual icon","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and if the label is still accessible to screen readers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Hiding a label is a design choice that must balance visual simplicity and clarity of intent, without compromising inclusiveness or form guidance.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"placeholder","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": if the text of the text input is empty a placeholder provides a hint or guidance inside the field to suggest expected input."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A prefix and a suffix can be added to give more context."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"leading icon"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": it helps indicate the purpose of the input (magnifying glass for search, envelope for email, phone device for phone number)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Only use a leading icon if it adds clear functional or contextual value."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"trailing action"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": it is used to provide actions related to the field: clear input, toggle password visibility, open a date picker, etc.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Can also indicate status or feedback (error checkmark, loading spinner).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Outlined-style","text":"Outlined style","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"default"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", the input is with a subtle background fill and invisible bottom border, creating a softer and more contained look.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Best suited for dense layouts or to enhance visibility."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"outlined"}]},{"type":"text","text":", the text input is a minimalist design with a transparent background and a visible stroke outlining the field."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This style may be interesting for contexts other than form pages:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When inputs need to feel lightweight and unobtrusive"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a header (search field)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a selection\/filtering feature in a product catalog"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"code":["   \/\/ An outlined text input","   OUDSTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text, isOutlined: true)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Rounded-layout","text":"Rounded layout","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Text input can have rounded layouts to be favored in more emotional, immersive contexts or those tied to specific visual identities."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For standard or business-oriented journeys, keep the default corners."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This evolution addresses the need for flexibility in adapting the design to some brand contexts."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To activate the rounded button behavior, set to true the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasRoundedTextInputs"},{"type":"text","text":" values of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tuning"},{"type":"text","text":" object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"in your theme configuration (if the theme exposes this property at init).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Some themes do not have this flexibility like ","type":"text"},{"code":"SoshTheme","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"WireframeTheme","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Status","anchor":"Status","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Five status are proposed for all layouts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"default (by default)","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Default neutral appearance, whether empty or filled."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It allows users to click, focus, and type freely without restrictions."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"error","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" status indicates that the user input does not meet validation rules or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expected formatting. It provides immediate visual feedback, typically through a red border,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error icon, and a clear, accessible error message positioned below the input. The error messages replaces the helper text."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"loading"}]},{"type":"text","text":": The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"type":"text","text":" state indicates that the system is processing or retrieving data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"related to the text entered. A progress indicator appears to inform the user that an action is in progress."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"readOnly","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" :The"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"readOnly"},{"type":"text","text":", lets the text visible but not editable"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"disabled","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": In "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"disabled"},{"type":"text","text":" status, the field is non-interactive and grayed out to indicate it cannot be changed."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Note the SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.disabled()"},{"type":"text","text":" is ignored."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Helpers","anchor":"Helpers"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Helper text"}]},{"type":"text","text":":  A supporting text conveys additional information about the input field,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as how it will be used. It should ideally only take up a single line, though may wrap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to multiple lines if required, and be either persistently visible or visible only on focus."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Helper link","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": If the helper text is not sufficient, it’s possible to offer the user","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an additional help link (the link can be external or open a modal)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Accessibility-considerations","type":"heading","text":"Accessibility considerations","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default no haptics are done by the component for the trailing action."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"However you should think about cases wher you will have to make the devices vibrates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can refer to the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/playing-haptics"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Mandatory-field-indication","type":"heading","text":"Mandatory field indication","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If all fields are mandatory (several fields present): display the message “All fields are mandatory” at the top of your formular."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Do not use an asterisk at the end of each field label, nor the word “mandatory.”"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If not all fields are mandatory (several fields present): display the message “All fields marked with an * are mandatory” at the top of your formular."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Use an asterisk (*) at the end of each mandatory field label, and ensures this is well vocalized."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"UI rendering of the asterisk must be done with ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"fbold font weight"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"negative content color","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (red-.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the mention “(optional)” at the end of each optional field label. Note that this rule is not systematic, it remains an option, to be used if needed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If there is only one field in the formular, or if the mandatory nature is obvious (such as login\/password),"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no mention is necessary since the fields are essential to the formular’s functionality.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Code-samples","type":"heading","text":"Code samples","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["    \/\/ The text to display and edit","    @State var text: String = \"\"","","    \/\/ Empty text and no placeholder","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text)","","    \/\/ Empty text with placeholder and suffix","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\", suffix: \"@orange.com\")","","    \/\/ Empty text with prefix and suffix","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, prefix: \"Distance\", suffix: \"km\")","","    \/\/ Add a leading icon for more context","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\", suffix: \"@orange.com\", leadingIcon: Image(systemName: \"envelope\"))","","    \/\/ Add a trailing button with local image namde \"ic_cross\" for additional action","    let trailingAction = OUDSTextInput.TrailingAction(icon: Image(\"ic_cross\"), actionHint: \"Delete\") { text = \"\" }","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, trailingAction: trailingAction)","","    \/\/ With helper text","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Email\",","                  text: $text,","                  placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\",","                  suffix: \"@orange.com\",","                  helperText: \"The email will be automatically completed with @orange.com\")","","    \/\/ With helper link","    @Environment(\\.openURL) private var openUrl","","    let helperLink = OUDSTextInput.HelperLink(text: \"Helper Link\") {","       openUrl.callAsFunction(url)","    }","","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text, placeholder: \"Placeholder\", helperLink: helperLink)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need to flip your icon depending to the layout direction or not (e.g. if RTL mode lose semantics  \/ meanings):"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["    @Environment(\\.layoutDirection) var layoutDirection","","    OUDSTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text, flipLeadingIcon: layoutDirection == .rightToLeft)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"Design documentation","anchor":"Design-documentation","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/r.orange.fr\/r\/S-ouds-doc-text-input"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Themes rendering","anchor":"Themes-rendering","level":2},{"type":"heading","text":"Orange","anchor":"Orange","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_Orange"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Orange Business Tools","anchor":"Orange-Business-Tools","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_OrangeBusinessTools"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Sosh","anchor":"Sosh","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_Sosh"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Wireframe","anchor":"Wireframe","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_textInput_Wireframe"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1.3.0 (Figma component design version)","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Version"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"0.20.0","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Since"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/oudscomponents\/oudstextinput"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://OUDSComponents/documentation/OUDSComponents/Controls":{"role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/Controls","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Some components can be used for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"controls","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"inputs","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Controls","url":"\/documentation\/oudscomponents\/controls","images":[{"id